<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Beloye</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as White Lake, Beloozero</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Beloye, the White Lake, is a large lake in Vologda Oblast in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, covering about 1,100 square kilometres. Its outflow, the Sheksna, runs south to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a>. The town of Beloozero, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belozersk">Belozersk</a>, stood on its shores, and the lake was part of the northern water routes linking the Volga with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-sea">White Sea</a> and the Baltic. Today it is part of the Volga-Baltic Waterway.</p></div>
